From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: clear the boot handshake before releasing the
 firmware

The firmware's reset handler spins until CTRL_INIT is non-zero, then
builds its memory map from the UC region registers and the ranges TZ
programmed in qcom_scm_mem_protect_video_var(), and reports the result
in CTRL_STATUS. The host writes CTRL_INIT only after authenticating the
image, protecting the memory and programming the UC region and queue
table, and then polls CTRL_STATUS. Neither side ever clears the two
registers. If they keep a value from an earlier firmware instance, for
example because the controller power domain did not collapse between
unload and reload, the new instance would start right after
qcom_scm_pas_auth_and_reset(), before the memory protection and the UC
region are set up, and could reject them as "invalid setting for
uc_region". A stale CTRL_STATUS can also be taken for the new
instance's answer.

On a cold boot, clear CTRL_INIT and CTRL_STATUS after powering the core
on and before the firmware is released, and warn when they were not
zero. The warm boot path is not changed.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c  |  2 ++
 .../platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c      | 23 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.h      |  1 +
 3 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
index 93b0a2bcfe..f8ec940515 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
@@ -106,6 +106,8 @@ static int __iris_core_init(struct iris_core *core)
 	if (ret)
 		goto error_queue_deinit;
 
+	iris_vpu_clear_boot_handshake(core);
+
 	ret = iris_fw_load(core);
 	if (ret)
 		goto error_power_off;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
index 25ae70dc27..14b8806e25 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
@@ -125,6 +125,29 @@ int iris_vpu_boot_firmware(struct iris_core *core)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The firmware's reset handler waits for CTRL_INIT before it reads the UC
+ * region and queue table registers, and then reports in CTRL_STATUS. Nothing
+ * else clears the two, so clear them before the firmware is released on a
+ * cold boot. A value left from an earlier firmware instance could otherwise
+ * start the new one before the host has programmed those registers, or be
+ * taken for its answer.
+ */
+void iris_vpu_clear_boot_handshake(struct iris_core *core)
+{
+	u32 ctrl_init, ctrl_status;
+
+	ctrl_init = readl(core->reg_base + CTRL_INIT);
+	ctrl_status = readl(core->reg_base + CTRL_STATUS);
+	if (!ctrl_init && !ctrl_status)
+		return;
+
+	dev_warn(core->dev, "stale boot handshake cleared: ctrl_init %#x ctrl_status %#x\n",
+		 ctrl_init, ctrl_status);
+	writel(0, core->reg_base + CTRL_INIT);
+	writel(0, core->reg_base + CTRL_STATUS);
+}
+
 void iris_vpu_raise_interrupt(struct iris_core *core)
 {
 	writel(1 << CPU_IC_SOFTINT_H2A_SHFT, core->reg_base + CPU_IC_SOFTINT);
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.h
index 09799a375c..f352f25f0f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.h
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ struct vpu_ops {
 };
 
 int iris_vpu_boot_firmware(struct iris_core *core);
+void iris_vpu_clear_boot_handshake(struct iris_core *core);
 void iris_vpu_raise_interrupt(struct iris_core *core);
 void iris_vpu_clear_interrupt(struct iris_core *core);
 int iris_vpu_watchdog(struct iris_core *core, u32 intr_status);
